        bf:subject              wd:Q128302279;
        bf:summary              "Largely considered the first modern artists' book, TwentySix Gasoline Stations is also the first bookwork by Ed Ruscha. Self-published in 1963 and in second and third editions in 1967 and 1969, Twentysix Gasoline Stations features black-and-white photos of gas stations taken from a distance along Route 66 in Southern California, Arizona, New Mexico, Oklahoma, and Texas, documenting the modernization of the American landscape and its expanding network of highways.--Printed Matter website.";
